   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi:\r<br>\r<br>You can use the limits = argument of a scale function to expand or\r<br>contract the limits. For example, if you do\r<br>\r<br>p + scale_x_reverse(limits = c(20, -5))\r<br>\r<br>just before the print(p) statement at the end, almost all the labeling\r<br>becomes visible, but you probably want that to be shaded in pink, so\r<br>you&#39;ll likely need to make a few adjustments in your code to allow\r<br>yourself that extra space.\r<br>\r<br>HTH,\r<br>Dennis\r<br>"
